A turn that ends pays for the rest of the tick, not for the counts it ran.
A thread that waits often would pay for time others ran, and run far less than its units;
a turn costs the counts it ran, so under tracing a call that moves no time costs nothing.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a tick did not cost the thread whose turn it was a tick less its units
Report: a traced call that moved no time charged the thread whose turn it was
Witness: fuzz lend-hands-turn

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -475,7 +475,7 @@ static uint32_t turn_close(void)
 #endif
     struct place *p = turn_place(core_self());
     if (p != NULL) {
-        p->balance -= turn_owes(p, offset);
+        p->balance -= turn_owes(p, timer_tick_counts());
     }
     return offset;
 }
